5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>About 6 in 10</strong><span class="t">rental and second-home tax bills go out of the area</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span><strong>30 days' notice</strong><span class="t">to leave after the first term</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge, 30+ years on the Grand Strand &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 6, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Five local fee schedules, a year of fees worked out, and when an owner needs a manager.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Four of the five property managers serving Horry County that print their fees take 10 percent of each month's rent on a yearly lease. Most add half a month to a full month's rent each time they place a new tenant. On a <span style="white-space:nowrap">3-bedroom</span> house renting for about $1,600 a month, that comes to about <span style="white-space:nowrap">$2,200 to $2,400</span> a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A vacation rental manager costs more. In the rentals we have seen, a basic plan takes about 13 to 17 percent of the bookings. Full service takes about 40 to 60 percent of the profit after costs, not of the bookings. Chapter3 does not manage property. We work out what you keep after the manager's fee.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Know the manager's real fee before you buy.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us run the numbers</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What managers charge</a></li><li><a href="#a-year" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Cost in a year</a></li><li><a href="#vacation-rentals" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Vacation rentals</a></li><li><a href="#do-you-need-one" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do you need one</a></li><li><a href="#extra-fees" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Fees on top</a></li><li><a href="#taxes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Rental taxes</a></li><li><a href="#the-law" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Contracts and the law</a></li><li><a href="#property-management-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Property management FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="fees"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What managers charge">How much do property managers charge in Myrtle Beach?</h2><style>
