stable, with a strong tourism industry and a growing job market. Vacancy rates are generally low, ensuring a steady stream of rental income. Additionally, investors should consider factors such as property management services, local regulations, and potential risks associated with hurricanes and natural disasters.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 2" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_illo-wrapper"><p class="tab-pane-title">Tenants and employers</p><p class="paragraph-17 tabs-content new-font">Myrtle Beach, SC is a popular coastal city with a population of approximately 34,000 people. The demographics of tenants in this area are diverse, ranging from families to young professionals and retirees. Known for its beautiful beaches and vibrant entertainment scene, Myrtle Beach attracts tourists from all over the world, making it an ideal location for short-term vacation rentals. Additionally, the city is home to a variety of major employers, including Horry County Schools, Tidelands Health, and Coastal Carolina University, providing job stability for residents and making it an attractive destination for long-term rental property investors.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 3" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_illo-wrapper"><p class="tab-pane-title">Rental laws and regulations</p><p class="paragraph-17 tabs-content new-font">In Myrtle Beach, South Carolina, the landlord-tenant laws and regulations are governed by the South Carolina Residential Landlord and Tenant Act. Landlords are required to provide habitable housing with essential amenities, and tenants have the right to report unsafe living conditions to government authorities. Lease agreements are legally binding contracts, and tenants must comply with the terms. Security deposits are allowed, and there is no specific limit set by state law. Landlords are obligated to disclose certain information to tenants, including authorized representatives and entry rights during the last 30 days of the tenancy.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 4" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_lilo-wrapper"><p class="tab-pane-title">Rental property management</p><p class="paragraph-17 tabs-content new-font">Long-term rental property management in Myrtle Beach, SC can offer a range of valuable services for property investors. These may include thorough tenant screening and selection processes, prompt rent collection and payment, regular property maintenance and repairs, effective marketing and advertising strategies, and detailed financial reporting. By taking care of these responsibilities, property management companies can assist investors in maximizing their rental income, reducing vacancies, and ensuring a smooth and profitable investment experience in the Myrtle Beach market.</p></div></div><div data-w-tab="Tab 5" class="tab_pane w-tab-pane"><div class="tab_lilo-wrapper"><p class="tab-pane-title">Properties and features</p><p class="paragraph-17 tabs-content new-font">In Myrtle Beach, SC, long-term rental property investors can find a range of property types including beachfront condos, single-family homes, and vacation rentals. Tenant-desired amenities often include ocean views, access to community pools or fitness centers, updated interiors, and proximity to popular attractions such as the boardwalk, golf courses, and shopping outlets. Additionally, properties with outdoor spaces, such as balconies or patios, are also highly sought after by tenants in this coastal city.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="w-embed"><style>
