+    <h1>How much does property management cost in <span class="r">Myrtle Beach</span>?</h1>
+    <p class="lead">Typically 8-12% of collected rent plus a stack of add-on fees. At Myrtle Beach&#039;s median rent of about $1,726/mo, the percentage alone runs roughly $2,071 per unit per year at 10%. A 10-unit portfolio pays about $20,712/yr before placement fees and markups. Here is the complete fee math, what those fees actually buy, and what it costs to run the office side with software instead.</p>
