+</section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="verdict"><b>The short version for Myrtle Beach:</b> at the median rent, every 10 units under management costs about $20,712 a year in percentage fees alone. Software that automates rent collection, late-payment follow-up, books, and owner reporting costs $1,788 a year flat. If you live in the area and can handle showings and the occasional inspection, the difference (about $18,924 a year on 10 units) is pay for work the software now does.</div></div></section><section class="faq">
