+<p class="faqs-heading">How is the license fee calculated?</p>
+<div class="faqs-toggle-content" style="display: none;"><p><p>Fees are calculated using the gross receipts of your business.&nbsp;&nbsp;Gross receipts are the total revenues generated by the business.&nbsp;&nbsp;Taxes collected for a governmental entity, or income which cannot be included for computation of the tax pursuant to State and Federal law are not deemed income and are exempt.&nbsp;&nbsp;Gross receipts from business done outside the city for which a license tax is paid to another municipality or county are also exempt.</p>
+<p>The license fee for a new business is calculated on an estimation of gross receipts from the first day of operation until May 31<sup>st</sup>.&nbsp;&nbsp;The reporting period for renewals is based on the preceding calendar or fiscal year.&nbsp;&nbsp;(Further information and instruction can be found on the reverse side of the business license application form.)</p></p>
+</div>
