+</b></div>
+<p class="faqs-heading">MISCELLANEOUS INFORMATION</p>
+<div class="faqs-toggle-content" style="display: none;"><p><p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Business Licenses are not transferable with a change of ownership.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A change of address must be reported to the Business License office within 10 days, and the business must be in compliance with zoning and building codes and any other City or State Codes.&nbsp;&nbsp;Failure to report the change of address shall invalidate the license, and the business can be prosecuted for operating without a business license.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;License fees are not refundable.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;License fees are not pro-rated.&nbsp;&nbsp;On the initial license application, gross receipts estimate is pro-rated based on the number of months remaining in the license year.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Non-resident businesses are charged only for business done within the city, but their rate is double the resident rate.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Certain home occupations are not permitted.&nbsp;&nbsp;(Please call the Zoning Department for more information.)</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Coin-operated vending and amusement machines require a city-issued decal in addition to any requirements of the SC Dept. of Revenue.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;General contractors, mechanical contractors (HVAC, Electrical, or Plumbing), residential builders, and residential specialty contractors must meet state standards and be licensed by the State of SC if required.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fire protection sprinkler contractors and alarm installers must be licensed by the State of SC.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Burglar alarm installers must be licensed by the State of SC.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Taxi owners must have a Certificate of Convenience and Necessity issued by the City, must provide proof of insurance to the City Risk Manager, and must have their vehicle inspected by the Police Department.</p>
+<p>&middot;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wrecker/Tow service operators must provide proof of insurance to the City Risk Manager and the wrecker/tow truck must be inspected by the Police Department.&nbsp;</p></p>
+</div>
